The VD55G0 is a 644x604 monochrome global shutter sensor from
STMicroelectronics. It streams Y8 or Y10 over one CSI-2 lane, runs its own
auto exposure, can strobe an illuminator from its GPIOs, and needs a
firmware patch at every power-on, carried in the driver as vd55g1 does.

The driver is ported from ST's own, GPL-2.0, to current interfaces: CCI
register access, .enable_streams with the subdev state, fwnode properties,
devm_v4l2_sensor_clk_get(), and an ACPI match for x86 machines where the
sensor sits behind ipu-bridge:
https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/vd55g0-linux-driver
ST's st,out-sync and st,in-sync and its two private controls are left out,
as vd55g1 has none of them. The supplies keep their DT names on ACPI too,
where int3472 maps them.

The clock tree is computed from the input clock and the one link frequency
the endpoint gives, as in vd55g1. The MIPI rate must be an integer multiple
of the input clock, or the sensor would run at another one, so any other
link frequency fails probe.

Exposure and the two gains form an auto cluster with auto exposure, as in
vd55g1: while auto exposure runs, they read back what the sensor applies.

Co-developed-by: Benjamin Mugnier <benjamin.mugnier@foss.st.com>
Signed-off-by: Benjamin Mugnier <benjamin.mugnier@foss.st.com>
Signed-off-by: Sergey Lebedev <lsa.uz@pm.me>
---
v5: no change.
v4: Sakari's review. The controls hold the settings, applied with
__v4l2_ctrl_handler_setup() at stream start and written by s_ctrl only
while powered; the subdev state holds the format and crop;
media_entity_is_streaming() replaces the driver's flag; one supply list,
which 3/6 maps on ACPI; and the smaller points. g_volatile_ctrl() still
sets ->val, as discussed on v3. Also the handler's lock is the state
lock, hflip and vflip form a cluster, AE_TARGET_PERCENTAGE is written as
16 bits, and LINE_LENGTH is written at stream start from the crop and
HBLANK. pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend() is no longer called: the core
does it since d1706f9da9f4, as Joshua Crofts's vd55g1 patch says.
v3: Sashiko's three points on v2 (auto exposure readback after a
stream, the runtime PM reference across probe, RUNTIME_PM_OPS() and
pm_ptr()); registration through v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor()
(Jizhou Tong), with dev_err_probe() on failure.
v2: no code change; MAINTAINERS no longer lists a binding for it.

